vasive and non-invasive ventilation and related equipment and supplies to patients suffering from COPD. It also sells and rents HME devices, such as non-invasive and invasive ventilators, positive airway pressure (PAP) machines, durable medical equipment, percussion vests, oxygen concentrators, and other medical equipment. In addition, the company provides neuromuscular care and oxygen therapy services; and sleep apnea management which provides sleep solutions and/or equipment, such as PAP, automatic continuous positive airway pressure, and bi-level positive airway pressure machines. Further, it offers in-home sleep apnea testing services; and breast pumps and related lactation equipment and supplies, including fulfillment and support services, as well as healthcare staffing and recruitment services. Viemed Healthcare, Inc. was founded in 2006 and is headquartered in Lafayette, Louisiana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Casey  Hoyt | CEO & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $181K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 22%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $8K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Viemed Healthcare, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $347M market cap on $270M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +25% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically. Gross margins of 61% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $12M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.48\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 26\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 14% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 23% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Valued at a 60% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Viemed Healthcare, Inc. (NASDAQ:VMD) Stock Has Average Target Price of $12.0